               compounds and a frustration factor (f) being significantly larger
               for Zn2MnSbO6 (f ≈ 20) compared to Zn2FeSbO6 (f ≈ 7). While
               Zn2FeSbO6 exhibits AFM ordering at a Néel temperature (TN) of 9
               K, Zn2MnSbO6 shows magnetic ordering around 4 K. Additionally,
               the negative Curie–Weiss temperatures for both compounds
