  journal   = "Adv. Opt. Mater.",
  publisher = "Wiley",
  volume    =  12,
  number    =  32,
  pages     =  2401437,
  abstract  = "AbstractDiscovery of new materials with enhanced optical
               properties in the visible and UV‐C range can impact applications
               in lasers, nonlinear optics, and quantum optics. Here, the
               optical floating zone growth of a family of rare earth borates,
               RBa3(B3O6)3 (R = Nd, Sm, Tb, Dy, and Er), with promising linear
               and nonlinear optical (NLO) properties is reported. Although
               previously identified to be centrosymmetric, the X‐ray analysis
               combined with optical second harmonic generation (SHG) assigns
               the noncentrosymmetric P space group to these crystals.
               Characterization of linear optical properties reveals a direct
               bandgap of ≈5.61–5.72 eV and strong photoluminescence in both the
               visible and mid‐IR regions. Anisotropic linear and nonlinear
               optical characterization reveals both Type‐I and Type‐II SHG
               phase matchability, with the highest effective phase‐matched SHG
